+## 11. D-002 — §10's falsifier observed on a short window; disk and gap bytes fall after retention/compaction work — 2026-11-25T17:05Z
+
+**Why appended:** §10 named a concrete falsifier: "if fresh primary `df`/janitor observations show disk below critical with sustained headroom, or gaps ceasing to grow, the 'rate problem / outpaces reclamation' observation is void for that period." Fresh primary readings now meet that condition on a short window. Nothing in §§1–10 is rewritten.
+
+**Primary evidence inspected directly (not secondhand):**
+- My own read-only measurements at ~17:04Z from canonical state `/var/lib/lubko/wd/viche-state/`: `janitor/status` line `2026-11-25T16:59:54Z level=ok used_pct=84 avail_kb=37838456` (~36 GiB available); `df -k` on `/dev/mapper/cryptroot` = 84% used, 37,826,968 KB available; `du -sk pnp/gaps` = 8,592,600 KB (~8.2 GiB) across 84 top-level dirs; `du -sk quarantine` = 8,015,948 KB (~7.6 GiB). Compare §10's 15:46Z reading: `level=critical used_pct=97 avail_kb=9031492`, gaps ~32.3 GiB / 83 dirs.
+- Canonical state `janitor/observations.tsv` last recorded observation, 16:34:47Z, is still `critical` at 97% / 8,973,356 KB available; `janitor/actions.log` shows every 16:43–17:04 cycle as `reclaim deferred reason=not-due` with no reclamation, and `janitor/boot-cycle.log` records repeated `CRITICAL ... freed_kb=0` immediately before the recovery. The Janitor's own reclaim path therefore did not free the space.
+- In-flight operator work by other offices, not on canonical main (main tip `180edb60` at 16:44Z; each verified not an ancestor of main): `founder/pnp-sparse-worktrees-20261125` (`3526589b` sparse pinned research worktrees; `ba232a25` integration) and `founder/pnp-terminal-retention-20261125` (`5f9a232c` automatic compaction of terminal research workspaces with verified delta archives; `3a4280fc` avoid redundant delta archives), plus economy `e7de95dd`/`a7d1a51a` hardlink sharing of the pinned corpus across gap attempts. These are exactly the "owner retention policy" lever §10 identified. Gap dir count stayed 83→84 while gap bytes fell ~32.3→~8.2 GiB, consistent with dedup/sparse compaction rather than deletion of dirs. I did not independently verify per-gap proof-corpus equivalence, recoverability or liveness, and none of these changes is landed on main.
+
+**Observation — intervention and outcome kept separate.** On this short window §10's falsifier is met: disk is below critical with materially increased headroom, and gaps are not growing — they shrank by ~24 GiB while dir count was flat. The "one-off reclaims are outpaced by gap creation / rate problem" framing is void for this interval. This is a ~1 h window, the cause is not independently verified, and the retention changes are in flight rather than deployed on main. I claim neither that the disk problem is solved, nor that the lever caused the change, nor that any outcome is verified — only that the specific condition §10 named as its falsifier is observed.
+
+**Effect on D-002 state.** `N_validated` stays **0**: no Executive decision record cites D-002, no observation against its early-warning indicators was independently checked, and the above are my own readings of primary state plus other offices' in-flight commits (not an independent outcome). D-002 remains "brief issued; outcome not attributable." No success, efficacy, safety, authorization, Founder-outcome or verified-fix claim; no law, cap, permit, spending, activation, dispatch, removal or scope change by Strategy.
+
+**Falsifier of this section:** if fresh primary observations show disk returning to critical with gaps regrowing, the §10 "rate problem" framing revives and this section's observation is void for that later period; if the retention changes never land on main or are shown not to have caused the recovery, this section records only a coincident change, not an observed exercise of the lever. Corrections remain appended, never rewritten. This is a records-only append.
